Doors are a nuisance. You never know when you are going to hit one..
Previously all doors/doorways were represented as '+'. I made minor
modifications to the code and now rooms look like this:

	------
	|....|
	|.....## <-- No door..
	|....| #
	--+---   <-- Open/closed/locked door..
	  #
	  #

Originally I wanted closed/locked doors to be hilited, but this is a much
harder task to accomplish, so this is an intermediate result. Perhaps when
3.1 is around and levl[][].color will be implemented.. (This was mentioned
in the code.)

Only normal dungeon levels are affected. At maze-levels the doors are 
handled as previously. The bug in zap.c--> When you zap a wand of digging
from corridor to the stone wall, the stone wall is not *visibly* affected.
Only when you walk on it, will it become visible. Now, it will become '#'
instantly.

Very very minor bug: When you are levitating over a trap-door and want
to go down with '>', nethack says:
"You're floating high above the ladder."
                                ^^^^^^
The diffs for doors and zap.c were posted to nethack-bugs. I didn't post
them here because they take about 340 lines. 

Also implemented:
When nethack creates a monster in the same room you are in, it now prints
messages like "There is a puff of smoke. A group of Hill-orcs appear."
These diffs were also posted to nethack-bugs.
